{"index":633,"node_id":"6c9d159e-e636-4c92-8fa1-4cfae1491cdd","parent":"5eda0d9c-c31b-42fb-9ddd-1f32fa48797f","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791081162.950816,"update_time":1791081162.950816,"content_type":"thoughts","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"thoughts\",\"thoughts\":[{\"summary\":\"Verified evaluation trigger, workflow runs, jobs, performance, status, and PASS results\",\"content\":\"\",\"chunks\":[],\"finished\":true}],\"source_analysis_msg_id\":\"cf33ee9e-c2f0-49fb-8484-df194dc2b6eb\"}"}
{"index":634,"node_id":"3ceed312-de1e-4722-901b-1797eff8a4c0","parent":"6c9d159e-e636-4c92-8fa1-4cfae1491cdd","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791081162.994989,"update_time":1791081162.994989,"content_type":"reasoning_recap","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"{\"content_type\":\"reasoning_recap\",\"content\":\"Worked for 52s\"}"}
{"index":635,"node_id":"3817a0dd-0adc-4933-93e8-e01c31d2a059","parent":"3ceed312-de1e-4722-901b-1797eff8a4c0","role":"assistant","author_name":null,"create_time":1791081163.015792,"update_time":1791081178.794186,"content_type":"text","status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":true,"recipient":"all","model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","default_model_slug":"gpt-5-6-thinking","part":1,"parts_total":1,"text":"I read the relevant section directly. You were correct; my previous representation was wrong.\n\nThe README says **`$key_object_literal:{}` and `$key_array_literal:[]` are decomposition operators, not output syntax**. The `_object_literal` and `_array_literal` suffixes **do not appear in the emitted JSON key**. fileciteturn131file0L2-L2\n\nSo this source:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"procedure\": {\n    \"step_contract\": {\n      \"step_0\": {\n        \"key\": \"start_of_turn\",\n        \"value\": \"ready\"\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nis explicitly decomposed by the README as:\n\n```json\n[\n  {},\n  {\"procedure\":{}},\n  {\"procedure\":{\"step_contract\":{}}},\n  {\"procedure\":{\"step_contract\":{\"step_0\":{}}}},\n  {\"procedure\":{\"step_contract\":{\"step_0\":{\"key\":\"start_of_turn\"}}}},\n  {\"procedure\":{\"step_contract\":{\"step_0\":{\"value\":\"ready\"}}}}\n]\n```\n\nSo `$key_object_literal:{}` means:\n\n```text\nGiven an object-valued property with actual key K,\nemit the atom:\n\n{ \"K\": {} }\n\nat that property's complete ancestral route.\n```\n\nNot:\n\n```json\n{\"K_object_literal\":{}}\n```\n\nLikewise, `$key_array_literal:[]` means that:\n\n```json\n{\"rule_following\":[\"A\",\"B\",\"C\"]}\n```\n\ndecomposes as:\n\n```json\n[\n  {},\n  {\"rule_following\":[]},\n  {\"rule_following\":[\"A\"]},\n  {\"rule_following\":[\"B\"]},\n  {\"rule_following\":[\"C\"]}\n]\n```\n\nThe initial `{}` is also significant: because the supplied value itself is an **unkeyed root object**, its own container atom is the bare object literal `{}`. An unkeyed root array analogously contributes `[]`. fileciteturn131file0L2-L2\n\nThere is another rule I missed: **anonymous intermediate containers are not automatically emitted as separate atoms.** For:\n\n```json\n{\"outer\":[{\"inner\":[\"A\",\"B\"]}]}\n```\n\nthe README gives:\n\n```json\n[\n  {},\n  {\"outer\":[]},\n  {\"outer\":[{\"inner\":[]}]},\n  {\"outer\":[{\"inner\":[\"A\"]}]},\n  {\"outer\":[{\"inner\":[\"B\"]}]}\n]\n```\n\nIt deliberately does **not** add:\n\n```json\n{\"outer\":[{}]}\n```\n\nbecause the `inner` atoms already establish that the array member is an object. But if the actual source were:\n\n```json\n{\"outer\":[{}]}\n```\n\nthen that empty object is itself information and **would** be retained. fileciteturn132file0L2-L2\n\nSo the precise principle is: **one atom adds exactly one new fact**, while whatever ancestral JSON structure is necessary to locate that fact is carried along without itself counting as additional payload facts."}
